{
 "about": "alpha_2 against the sigma_v (Fingers-of-God) dispersions as a function of the scale cut, per bin layout. one_minus_f_least_redundant_group: 1 - f for the alpha_2 group template that the sigma_v templates reproduce least, f = 1 - min_c (a - S c)^T C^-1 (a - S c)/(a^T C^-1 a) on the band powers the cut keeps; one_minus_f_alpha2_12p5_all_groups: the same for alpha_2 equal in every group. rho_max: the largest |correlation| between an alpha_2 parameter and a sigma_v in the posterior of model B + tilts on the pessimistic linear-bias prior (priors included). fom_ratio_alpha2_fixed: FoM_{alpha_2 = 0}/FoM, FoM(w0, wa) of that model with alpha_2 and its tilts fixed at 0 over FoM with alpha_2 free (_flat_sigma_v: sigma_v priors also removed). shift_ratio_*: delta_{sigma_v free}/delta_{sigma_v fixed}, with delta the shift of model A + tilts on the pessimistic prior (no alpha_2) fitted to the truth alpha_2 = 12.5 h^-2 Mpc^2 in every group ((w0, wa) in its ellipse, Omega_m and A_s in their sigma), sigma_v free on its Gaussian prior (_prior) or flat (_flat), over sigma_v fixed at the fiducial. k_max is the z = 0 value of a per-bin cut at k_max/D(zbar_i). None: no band kept. Written by EXAMPLE_EVALUATE_FISHER_MODEL_B.ipynb (section 11, final-tier caches).",
